      <div class="s"><div class="k">{{ t('Net since launch','上线以来净流入') }}</div><div class="v" style="font-size:18px">${{ etf.cum_usd_bn }}B</div><div class="h">{{ etf.cum_btc_str }}</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="sub" style="margin-top:10px">{{ t('Measured (2024→, ETF era only — so CONFIRMATION-grade, not a both-halves anchor): strong net inflows (flow z 0.25–0.75) preceded +5.0%/30d and +12.2%/90d at 65% hit, while strong outflows (z below −0.75) preceded −2.9%/30d. The relationship is intuitive and DIRECTIONAL, but only ~2.4 years exist, so it confirms the risk read rather than leading it. An integration A/B (reports/vector-integration-candidates.md) keeps it here as risk context, NOT in the allocation math — the continuous flow-z is the cleaner drawdown read, and wiring the discrete accumulation/distribution state into the strategy did not survive the both-halves test. Glassnode-sourced via BGeometrics, free.', '实测（2024 起，仅 ETF 时代 — 故为确认级，而非双半段锚点）：强净流入（资金流 z 0.25–0.75）后 30 天 +5.0%、90 天 +12.2%、胜率 65%；强净流出（z 低于 −0.75）后 30 天 −2.9%。关系直观且具方向性，但仅约 2.4 年样本，故用于确认风险判断而非领先。一项整合 A/B（reports/vector-integration-candidates.md）将其保留为风险背景，而非并入仓位计算 — 连续的资金流 z 是更干净的回撤读数，而将离散的吸筹/派发状态写入策略未能通过双半段检验。数据经 BGeometrics 源自 Glassnode，免费。') }}</div>
    {% endif %}
